<title>UK: Stolt Comex gets $68 mln Brazil contract.</title>
<headline>Stolt Comex gets $68 mln Brazil contract.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Subsea contractor Stolt Comex Seaway said on Tuesday it had been awarded a four-year, $68 million contract by Brazilian state oil company Petrobras.</p>
<p>The contract, for work on Brazil's deepwater offshore Campos Basin oilfield, will start in May 1997.</p>
<p>Stolt Comex will provide the vessel Seaway Harrier for diving and remote-controlled subsea operations.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 542 8060</p>
</text>
